/* BSharp (or simply B#) is a multi-endpoints programming language 
that can be interpreted, compiled, and transpiled into C++ and Dlang.
It features high presicion mathematical computation functions and
algorithms in addition to a very flexable and dynamic typing methods.
B-Sharp is strong for mathematical computations, graphics computations,
graphical user interface applications, and even server applications 
thanks to its very large standard library. It also comes with built-in
support for machine and deep learning algorithms, in addition to other
useful built-in language modules such as a very rich regular experssions
engine, and a powerful file-system operations module. */

/* This file matches EX-Standards for B-Sharp: EX99 Standards */

// This file was first written by Bahaa Nofal 29/Sept/2026

module f90.bsharp

!pragma enforce         // Enforce types across this file
!pragma optimize        // Optimization algorithms invoked

// BSHARP_IMPORT_LIBS
using "Compiler/optimize.bsharp"        // Optimization Algorithms
using "Alogirthms/datatypes.bsharp"     // Additional Datatypes
using "Algorithms/algorithms.bsharp"    // Data Algorithms
